   - FIX: pastoral_burden() and theological_lane() for epistle now include reference in template
     so adjacent days with same key_terms still produce distinct text
   - Expected new scores: John 10 ~100 (application_unanchored: 0), Romans 5 ~74+ (less deductions)

2. WRITER FLAT (40-55 forever):
   - training_corpus._candidate_meta_paths() was hardcoded to a single old 2026-03-14 Proverbs artifact
   - Same artifact evaluated every cycle → LLM evaluator varies slightly (LLM non-determinism) but
     content is fixed → scores oscillate 40-55 with no improvement possible
   - FIX: _candidate_meta_paths() now returns all metas sorted newest-first
   - Training cycle will now evaluate the most recent pipeline output
   - Expected outcome: scores will reflect actual current pipeline quality as it improves

Both fixes are in src/autoresearch/ — will take effect on the next training cycle.

